A||N||13||87ECO5||Is this borderline "ricer"?||||6||
Z||000000||87ECO5||08-28-2000||12:59 PM||||Did some more cosmetic work to my coupe.  Couldn't wait to get the photos back so I could post them here.<P>First photo shows it all:  new bra, freshly-painted sail panels with decals and a "Ferrari 360 wannabe" crest decal on the left fender:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_360_wannabe_2.jpg"> <P>I've hated those stupid Pontiac "arrowhead" emblems on the sail panels since day one.  So, I called up Paul McKibben and asked him to help me out.  We came up with this idea:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_sail_1.jpg"> <P>Since making such small cuts in vinyl can be tricky for the machine that does this work, Paul did a few trial runs first.  He ended up sending me three good decals (he only charged me for two!).  So, I think I came up with a good place to put the third decal:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_bra_1.jpg"> <P>Here's a close-up shot of those decals:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_pegasus_1.jpg"> <P>Call me crazy, but I've always liked those yellow crests found on the new Ferrari 360.  And when I found out that Paul made one for the Fiero, well, I had to have one:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_crest_1.jpg"> <P>Finally, here's the proud father with his baby:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_proud_dad_1.jpg"> <P>It's very important that I take a moment to thank Paul McKibben.  Without him, this would not have been possible.  Paul was absolutely incredible to work with.  I <B>HIGHLY</B> recommend him!<P>So ... what do you think?  Is it approaching "ricer" status?<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||BENGAL4||08-28-2000||01:14 PM||||I think with that hat, I would mistake you for a ricer. But with that head, you should wear a hat. JK.<P> The car looks great. One question, does the decals make it go faster?||||reg||10
Z||000002||bHooper||08-28-2000||01:22 PM||||yea,  what are the performance gains?  was there any "break in time"?<P>btw, the car looks good<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||08-28-2000||01:40 PM||||Lookin' good Scott !!! Not you...the car...lol||||reg||14
Z||000004||fiero56||08-28-2000||03:09 PM||||Looking good, Scott. I wasn't sure how that fender sticker would look when you mentioned thinking about putting one on. But, I have to say it looks very good on there.<BR>Plus, after seeing your sail panels in person, I don't think I like the Pontiac "arrow-heads" either. How about the "Pontiac" on the rear fascia, whats going on with that?<P>Scott's ricer mods:<BR>- calipers are painted red<BR>- wheels are painted black<BR>- engine has been painted red with yellow oil dipstick<BR>- bra<BR>- sail panel stickers<BR>- Pontiac rear fascia sticker<BR>- fender sticker<BR>- guage stickers<BR>- short shifter<BR>- painted ashtrays<BR>- painted engine grills<BR>- bra sticker<BR>Thats about all I can think of right now<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||08-28-2000||03:22 PM||||Where'd you get those fender stickers?||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||08-28-2000||04:27 PM||||Those are the exact fender stickers I was looking for to put on my Fiero F-50 when it is completed.  <P>Paul, are you out there?  How much?||||reg||1
Z||000007||RiceCooker||08-28-2000||06:51 PM||||wait, wait, wait,<BR>Let's get this straight. The hat goes BACKWARDS! HA! HA! HA!<P>seriously though, i love the sail panel decals||||reg||6
Z||000008||87ECO5||08-28-2000||08:16 PM||||No, I didn't get a horsepower increase.  In fact, if you consider the added weight and the more wind resistance from the edges of all that vinyl, I've actually slowed my car down!  What was I thinking!!!???     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Drew:  Thanks for the nice comments.  Your list just about covers everything I've done.  Regarding the "PONTIAC" emblem on the rear fascia ... Formula had made me a nice one but my youngest daughter got ahold of it (and a few other things) and shredded it.  So, I asked Paul to make me one.  It's on its way now.<P>GT Bastard and mshill:  The fender crest logo came from Paul McKibben also.  For the two-color decal, he charged me $13 (including shipping).<P>RiceCooker:  Thanks.  I put together a small thread in the Technical section on how I did the sail panels.  Here's the link:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005467.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005467.html</A> <P>BTW, I was disappointed with the original scans so I rescanned the photos and added some effects to enhance the pictures somewhat.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||BOILERMAKER||08-28-2000||10:07 PM||||It looks great.  I can't wait to get mine painted and put it next to yours.  Of course, I will have to do a LOT of work to get mine even close to the condition yours is in.  Then maybe I will hire you to do some decal work on mine.<P>Get that Northstar in yours ... no wait, get that NORTHSTAR in mine ... no wait, OH, just keep the 4 banger.  LOL||||reg||1
Z||000010||Gokart||08-29-2000||10:18 PM||||Looks awesome! Personal touches are not "ricey" IMHO unless your advertising something you don't have(V-tec,turbo,etc). You are proudly displaying the Fiero emblem <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Fart can exhausts would get you on Brian's page though <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||08-29-2000||10:40 PM||||Honestly, <P>I can think of no better picture of a car than with its proud owner who made it look good. <P>Subtle is good, its the subtle things in life that are sometimes the most noticeable.||||reg||1
